# PlantUML Diagram Generation Configuration

This directory contains PlantUML class diagrams for the OCI DevOps project components.

## Level 3 Components Covered

### Controllers (6 diagrams)
- `Controllers/AuthController.puml` - Authentication controller
- `Controllers/TaskController.puml` - Task management controller
- `Controllers/DashboardController.puml` - Dashboard view controller
- `Controllers/UserController.puml` - User management controller
- `Controllers/ToDoItemController.puml` - ToDo item CRUD operations
- `Controllers/ToDoItemBotController.puml` - Telegram bot integration

### Services (3 diagrams)
- `Services/GeminiService.puml` - Google Gemini AI integration
- `Services/TelegramSummaryService.puml` - Telegram summary generation
- `Services/TelegramMessageService.puml` - Telegram message handling

### Repositories (5 diagrams)
- `Repositories/UserRepository.puml` - User data persistence
- `Repositories/TaskRepository.puml` - Task data persistence
- `Repositories/TelegramMessageRepository.puml` - Telegram message storage
- `Repositories/TelegramSummaryRepository.puml` - Telegram summary storage
- `Repositories/ToDoItemRepository.puml` - ToDo item storage

## Generating Diagrams

To generate all Level 3 component diagrams, run the PlantUMLDiagramGenerator utility:

```bash
# From the backend directory
cd MtdrSpring/backend

# Compile the project (if not already compiled)
mvn clean compile

# Run the diagram generator
mvn exec:java -Dexec.mainClass="com.springboot.MyTodoList.util.PlantUMLDiagramGenerator"
```

The generator will:
1. Scan each component's Java package
2. Generate PlantUML class diagrams for all classes in that package
3. Save each diagram to its own `.puml` file in organized subdirectories
4. Display generation status and any errors

